From 3cd0faa9ba07cc520c8e57bc5342d59660313753 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 19:31:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_bcm4377: require only beamforming calibration
 on BCM4388

BCM4388 always uploads the beamforming calibration through
bcm4388_send_calibration(). Do not reject its device-tree configuration
when the unused non-beamforming calibration property is absent.

Keep the beamforming blob mandatory and retain the existing calibration
requirements for other chips. Calibration still comes exclusively from
the device tree; this does not add a firmware-file fallback.

Validation: the hci_bcm4377 driver object builds for arm64 with LLVM.

Assisted-By: OpenAI Codex (GPT-6 Astra)
Signed-off-by: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c
index 0eb137a99add7..f379b08aa7d2b 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c
@@ -2228,6 +2228,10 @@ static int bcm4377_probe_of(struct bcm4377_data *bcm4377)
 	bcm4377->taurus_beamforming_cal_blob =
 		of_get_property(np, "brcm,taurus-bf-cal-blob",
 				&bcm4377->taurus_beamforming_cal_size);
+	if (bcm4377->hw->id == 0x4388) {
+		/* BCM4388 never uses the non-beamforming calibration. */
+		return bcm4377->taurus_beamforming_cal_blob ? 0 : -ENOENT;
+	}
 	if (!bcm4377->taurus_beamforming_cal_blob) {
 		dev_err(&bcm4377->pdev->dev,
 			"no brcm,taurus-bf-cal-blob property\n");
-- 
